                <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='9'>: A married senior male (ID: 648220867) with a high school education tops with $69,998 in claims, followed by an unmarried senior male (ID: 478701858) with $63,326.</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='9'>Vans</run>
                <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='9'>: An unmarried senior male (ID: 821927891) with a high school education leads with $73,783. Two elderly males follow, filing $64,448 and $64,182, respectively.</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='9'>Panel Trucks</run>
                <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='9'>: The highest claimant is a married, middle-aged male (ID: 916006924) with less than a high school education, filing $88,193. Second is an unmarried senior male (ID: 259402525) with a bachelor’s degree, filing $67,361.</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='9'>Car Age Insights</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='9'>Cars purchased in 2024 (age 1) have the highest total claims, regardless of usage type: $7.2M for commercial and $5.4M for private vehicles.</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
