            <customized-tooltip>
              <formatted-text>
                <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='9'>Key Insights</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='9'>Top Professions for Claims</run>
                <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='9'>: Blue-collar professionals lead in total claims, followed by clerical workers, while doctors report the lowest claim amounts.</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='9'>Gender Split</run>
                <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='9'>: Females account for </run>
                <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='9'>55.63%</run>
                <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='9'> of total claims, outpacing males.</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='9'>Urban vs. Rural</run>
                <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='9'>: The majority of claims (</run>
                <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='9'>93.84%</run>
                <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='9'>) come from urban areas, with rural areas contributing only </run>
                <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='9'>6.16%</run>
                <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='9'>.</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='9'>Education Factors</run>
                <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='9'>: Drivers with </run>
                <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='9'>high school</run>
                <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='9'> or </run>
                <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='9'>bachelor&apos;s degrees</run>
                <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='9'> show higher claim frequencies, while those with a </run>
                <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='9'>PhD</run>
                <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='9'> are the least likely to make claims.</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='9'>Most Vulnerable Demographics</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='9'>Male Manager</run>
                <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='9'> with a high school education holds the highest average total claim of </run>
                <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='9'>$9,440</run>
                <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='9'>.</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='9'>Male Homemaker</run>
                <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='9'> with a master’s degree follows with an average claim of </run>
                <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='9'>$8,590</run>
                <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='9'>.</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='9'>Male Homemaker</run>
                <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='9'> with a high school education reports an average claim of </run>
                <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='9'>$8,193</run>
                <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='9'>.</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='9'>Male Blue-Collar Worker</run>
